    "source_evidence": [
      {
        "source": "F0003:S3:T1:A1",
        "quote": "SECONDARY, LOW CONFIDENCE: multi-species PK table adapted from Roffey et al. 2003"
      },
      {
        "source": "F0003:S3:T1:A2",
        "quote": "S01 | No DOI; de Araujo BV 2008 doctoral thesis, UFRGS, lume.ufrgs.br/bitstream/handle/10183/12602/000628550.pdf | Tabela 2.5 / \"Tabela 5.\" p.26; adapted from Roffey SJ et al. Drug Metab Dispos 2003;31:731-741, DOI 10.1124/dmd.31.6.731 (original not accessed)"
      },
      {
        "source": "F0003:S3:T1:A3",
        "quote": "SECONDARY SOURCE. A thesis reproduction of Roffey 2003 (\"Adaptado de ROFFEY et al., 2003\"); the original paper was not available, so no value here has been checked against it. Treat every value as low confidence."
      },
      {
        "source": "F0003:S3:T1:A4",
        "quote": "Title: \"Parâmetros farmacocinéticos do voriconazol em diversas espécies animais.\" Header as extracted has 5 species names (Camundongo | Rato | Coelho | Cobaio | Cão) but 6 data columns, because rat has male and female columns."
      },
      {
        "source": "F0003:S3:T1:A5",
        "quote": "Column mapping by header order is NOT_VERIFIED: col1 mouse, col2 rat male, col3 rat female, col4 rabbit, col5 guinea pig, col6 dog. Two text extractions gave opposite n for col4 and col5 (rabbit n = 1 and guinea pig n = 3, or the reverse). The dog binding of 51% is also quoted in a horse study."
      },
      {
        "source": "F0003:S3:T1:A6",
        "quote": "Footnote: \"*=Ligação as Proteínas Plasmáticas; u = dose única; m = dose múltipla (uma vez ao dia por 10 dias), exceto para cobaio (3 vezes ao dia).\" ASC = AUC; LPP = plasma protein binding (%). Decimal commas are Portuguese (41,7 means 41.7)."
      },
      {
        "source": "F0003:S3:T1:A7",
        "quote": "\"f\" has no unit or definition in the table; two values exceed 100. AUC end time t, multiple-dose sampling day, formulation and matrix are not given."
      },
